+# ---------------- Shared - coordinate space conversion ----------------
+# [MP8] ⚠️⚠️ Converts "move dist meters along world x" into **an offset in the parent node's local coordinates**.
+#
+# This was the real culprit behind "4 players fall into a black void" in v3's first version (tracked down in testing on 2026-08-16).
+# `light parent` has a **-135.7° Y rotation** in the scene (measured by probe31 from the stock PCK),
+# and `position` is in the parent's local coordinates. Writing `od.position = o.position + Vector3(120,0,0)`
+# means moving along its **rotated** x axis — the 4 omni lights got flung over to world (-86, 0, +84),
+# leaving the second venue with no lights at all. And in this scene `ambient_light_source` = background color (0,0,0),
+# and both DirectionalLight3D nodes are `visible = false` — **no lights means a pitch-black void**,
+# even with geometry / tracks / spawn points / camera all correct (nailed down by three tables from probe29 + probe30 + probe31).
+#
+# Rule of thumb - before writing any `dup.position = src.position + offset`, first ask
+# **"is this parent's basis the identity?"** In this scene, three of them aren't.
+# `light parent` (rotated -135.7°), `sequence_label_scene_parent` (scaled 0.818),
+# `CameraTarget` (rotated -43.7°/26.8°, but its position is in root space, so it's unaffected).
+#
+# ⚠️ You can't use `global_transform` here. This function runs in the root's `_enter_tree()`,
+# when the children aren't in the tree yet and global transforms are unreliable — so it multiplies the **local** basis level by level.
+# ⚠️ The parameter is `Node`, not `Node3D`, because `Minigame` isn't a subclass of Node3D.
+# Typing it as Node3D makes `_mp8_local_delta(self)` a Parse Error **at load time** —
+# and gdre's "compiles fine" check can't catch this kind of type error. In game it shows up as **a fully black screen** (the whole script fails to load).
+func _mp8_local_delta(node: Node, world_delta: Vector3) -> Vector3 :
+
+	if node == null or node == self:
+		return world_delta
+
+	var b := Basis.IDENTITY
+	var cur: Node = node
+	while cur != null and cur != self:
+		if cur is Node3D:
+			b = (cur as Node3D).transform.basis * b
+		cur = cur.get_parent()
+
+	return b.inverse() * world_delta
+
+
+# A node's world x — again `global_position` can't be used (not in the tree yet during `_enter_tree`),
+# so it's computed by multiplying its own local transforms up the chain level by level.
+func _mp8_world_x(node: Node) -> float :
+
+	var chain: Array[Node3D] = []
+	var cur: Node = node
+	while cur != null and cur != self:
+		if cur is Node3D:
+			chain.push_front(cur as Node3D)
+		cur = cur.get_parent()
+
+	var t := Transform3D.IDENTITY
+	for n in chain:
+		t = t * n.transform
+	return t.origin.x
+
+
+# [MP8] Light self-check (runs after entering the tree) - logs each cloned light's **world offset** from its original.
+# Expected exactly (±step, 0, 0). Off by more than 0.5 m means the coordinate space pitfall was hit again, and the log marks it ❌.
+func _mp8_verify_lights() -> void :
+
+	for od in _mp8_light_check:
+		if not is_instance_valid(od) or not od.is_inside_tree():
+			continue
+		var src_name := String(od.name).trim_suffix("_MP8L").trim_suffix("_MP8R")
+		var src: Node3D = od.get_parent().get_node_or_null(NodePath(src_name)) as Node3D
+		if src == null:
+			continue
+		var d: Vector3 = od.global_position - src.global_position
+		var ok: bool = absf(absf(d.x) - _mp8_step) < 0.5 and absf(d.y) < 0.5 and absf(d.z) < 0.5
+		print("[MP8] Escalator Pit: cloned light %-18s world=(%8.2f,%7.2f,%8.2f)  offset from original=(%7.2f,%6.2f,%7.2f)  expected ±%.2f  %s" % [
+			od.name, od.global_position.x, od.global_position.y, od.global_position.z,
+			d.x, d.y, d.z, _mp8_step, "OK" if ok else "❌ light didn't follow!"
+		])
+
+# [MP8] Tried and failed, written down so nobody tries again - **narrowing players' arms by moving IK targets does nothing at all.**
+# Players already have `ik target_left/right hand`, so in theory moving them should change the pose. In testing, squeezing the factor down to
+# `mp8escarm=0.05` (both hands together at the chest) **didn't change a single pixel** (comparison shot esc8_arm005) —
+# the pose is written into the skeleton every frame by `character_animation_tree`, so SkeletonIK3D's result gets overwritten by the animation and can't take effect.
+# (This was a workaround thought up in v2, when "lanes were squeezed to 2.737 m and fingertips were only 0.16 m apart". In v4 lane spacing is back to vanilla's
+#   6.4 m, so it isn't cramped. **This problem doesn't exist in v4**, and this note is kept only to remember the conclusion that "IK can't change the pose".)
+
